          {
            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "Phymosia umbellata is a species of flowering plant in the family Malvaceae. It is native to Mexico and is cultivated as an ornamental plant."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "This tropical evergreen shrub grows to {{cvt|3|m|ft|abbr=on}} in height, with cup shaped scarlet flowers produced mainly in summer."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "In temperate areas it requires a warm, sheltered position."
          }
